Greetings, Officers!

After reviewing your feedback, we updated the Zombie Case DLC to make the gameplay more enjoyable for you:

[list]
[*] Made the zombies slightly weaker than before, but they're still a serious threat;
[*] Redesigned zombie missions:
a) Changed zombie spawners and suspects;
b) Overall, there are more zombies and civilians, but fewer bandits;
c) Some rooms now only have zombies in them;
[*] Fixed a bug with using a defibrillator on a partner in cooperative mode;
[*] Missions will now not end as long as at least one infected person remains on the map to avoid conflicts at the end of the level;
[/list]
We tried for you, so thanks again for the feedback!

P.S. And don't forget to add the free Police Stories: The Academy prologue to your wishlist, which will be out soon!

https://store.steampowered.com/app/1986760/Police_Stories_The_Academy/

Greetings, Officers!

While work on Police Stories: The Academy continues, we're polishing up what we've already released. In particular, a lot of work is being done on the Zombie Case DLC:

[list]
[*] Fixed an issue with the partition wall display on the left side of mission 12 of the main campaign;
[*] Fixed an issue with passability in the sofa area in the first Zombie Case mission;
[*] Fixed zombie spawning, now the "heaviest" zombies will not spawn in the first levels of Zombie Case;
[*] Fixed a problem with evidence spawning in some missions;
[*] Slightly reduced zombie health to make it a little easier to deal with them.
[/list]
We listened to your criticism of the DLC, so there are still more balance tweaks to be made to the Zombie Case DLC in the future.

And don't forget to add the free Police Stories: The Academy prologue to your wishlist, which will be out soon!

https://store.steampowered.com/app/1986760/Police_Stories_The_Academy/

