Greetings, officers!

We’ve been preparing this Police Stories version for a long time. An updated partner with improved AI. A new police story telling about a crazy anarchist Charlie McDennis. Finally, a Halloween mode in which you’ll meet the long-awaited zombies for the first time.

[h2]1. Partner with a switchable behaviour[/h2]

[h3]Passive mode[/h3]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/20908442385faf8fdf8a4eaf45c423b0d3b70680.gif[/img]

[list]
[*] Enabled by default;
[*] The partner behaves as before, acting strictly on the player’s orders;
[*] The partner will pay attention to the points of potential threat;
[*] If the partner is left idle (not on the order), he will return to the player.
[/list]

[h3]Active mode[/h3]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/da6395b157f5a44b87f845ed7c80a879adeaedbc.gif[/img]

[list]
[*] The partner will stand still only by the order of the player, in other cases he will return to the player automatically;
[*] The partner himself looks at the points of potential threat, from where the suspects are expected to appear;
[*] When meeting a suspect, the partner now independently takes actions to neutralize them if the player is not nearby:
[olist]
[*] Asks them to surrender;
[*] In case of disobedience, he uses physical force;
[*] In case of aggressive resistance, uses a weapon;
[*] If a suspect starts to run away, the partner will pursue them as long as he considers it safe;
[*] Picks up weapons dropped from suspects;
[/olist]
[*] If the suspect gives themselves away, the partner will be ready for their actions;
[*] The player's commands have the highest priority unless a suspect is raising a weapon.[/list]

[h2]2. New campaign “The Story of Charlie McDennis”[/h2]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/ea8e7b6a84eae1c854b7e1e8e75c2efa4c377369.jpg[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/1f85e87ebaa8e03bef48eadfb273d766b48b1003.jpg[/img]

[list]
[*] The new campaign opens after completing the main one, its story begins after John's first working day with Rick;
[*] Five new missions, which we have slightly redone from the previous beta.
[/list]

[h2]3. Halloween Mode[/h2]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/a818c6b9b38781f452fb98c5a3c6613decdde629.gif[/img]
[list]
[*] Theme decorations and a zombie character;
[*] You can switch it from the main menu;
[*] We advise you to play the new campaign without the zombie mode on first;
[*] 
[*] Zombie Character:
[olist]
[*] Attacks the nearest person, regardless of whether they are a policeman or a suspect;
[*] You must save the suspects who haven’t picked up their weapons from the zombies, otherwise you will be charged with unjustified violence;
[*] Find your way to deal with an unexpected threat.
[/olist][/list]

Make sure to share your impressions of the zombies! We plan to create a full-fledged zombie mode, which will significantly differ from the current one. We hope you like the new features!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/2fa6ae6e86b7a92db0fe1c508c16c15fc8f246c8.png[/img]

Yes, it's another Beta branch update! Most likely it's the final one before we move it to the public. That's why it's more important than ever for more people to check it to make sure everything is top-notch.

Based on your feedback, we decided to give players the ability switch the partner AI behavior on the go.

[h2]You can now access 1.4.2 Beta Version through Steam by choosing it in the BETAS tab (Right-click on the game in your library > Properties > Betas > Select open-beta > Download the update).
[/h2]

Beta 1.4.2 is full of new features:

[h3]New campaign is updated[/h3]
[list]
[*] The new story becomes available after completing the main campaign;
[*] All new missions are slightly reworked from the last beta version;
[/list]
[h3]Partner character can now switch behavioral modes.[/h3]

[b]Passive mode is enabled by default: [/b]
[list]
[*] The partner acts strictly at the player's command, not performing any autonomous actions. 
[*] The partner will now notify players of potential threat points;
[*] If the partner is left idle (no orders given), he will return to the player-controlled character;
[/list]

[b]When you point the cursor at your partner and press the ‘orders’ key, you can activate your partner's ‘aggressive mode’[/b]
[list]
[*] The partner will only stand still when ordered by the player, otherwise he will always return to the player-controlled character automatically;
[*] The partner is on lookout for points of potential threat, from where suspects might appear;
[*] Encountering a suspect, Rick will automatically take action to disarm him, if the player-controlled character isn’t close by:
[list][*] He first orders him to surrender;
[*] He uses physical force if suspect doesn’t comply;
[*] If the suspect becomes aggressive or resists arrest, Rick might apply lethal force;
[*] If a suspect decides to flee, Rick will chase him for as long as he thinks its safe;
[*] Rick will automatically pick up weapons dropped by suspects;[/list]
[*] If a suspect has given himself away, Rick will be ready for to take action;
[*] Player’s commands have the highest priority except for the times the suspects take up arms.
[/list]

The partner AI turned out to be a major challenge, and we wanted to have a well-polished feature. A few delays had to be made for better player experience. We hope you enjoy Rick's switchable behavior.

Enjoy the game!

