Greetings, officers!

We received a lot of useful feedback on the new AI partner. Taking into account your comments and analyzing the situation, we decided to make a few more changes.

The main guideline in these changes to the partner was that we wanted to make him a second player able to act autonomously, but still be dependent on the main player. We overdid it a bit with his aggressiveness, so we made him a little weaker.

While we are improving the partner, we invite you to play the updated beta, which includes all the innovations that we were going to release with the update.

[h3]You can now access 1.4.0 Beta Version through Steam by choosing it in the BETAS tab (Right-click on the game in your library > Properties > Betas > Select open-beta > Download the update).[/h3]

Please fill in this form to help us improve the game: https://forms.gle/ZofakzVNdKg9eRKa9

[h2]Five new missions.[/h2]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/22cca3d21445e5d92b1a2066100f535e8e1a5ac9.jpg[/img]
[list]
[*] A new campaign opens after completing the main one;
[*] Five new cards revealing more opportunities and developing the game’s aspect with destructible walls;
[*] The story begins after John's first working day with Rick.
[/list]

[h2]Smart partner[/h2]For now, we keep the changes from the previous version of the beta test.
[list]
[*] The partner will stand still only by the order of the player, in other cases he will return to the player automatically;
[*] The partner looks at the points of a potential threat himself — the places from where the suspects are expected to appear;
[*] When meeting a suspect, the partner now independently takes actions to neutralize them:
[list]
[*] Asks them to surrender;
[*] In case of disobedience, he uses physical force;
[*] In case of aggressive resistance, uses a weapon;
[*] If the suspect starts to run away, the partner will pursue him as long as he considers it safe;
[*] Picks up weapons dropped from suspects;[/list]
[*] If the suspect gives themselves away, the partner will be ready for their actions;
[*] The player's commands have the highest priority unless the suspect is raising a weapon;
[/list]
New changes:
[list]
[*] Reduced the partner's accuracy;
[*] Reduced the reaction speed of the partner;
[*] The partner no longer fires at stunned targets.
[/list]

Thanks to you, we have the strength and inspiration to develop this project further. Therefore, we ask you to take part in a survey about the "smart" partner and the new campaign.

Thank you for sharing your thoughts and wishes! We are working on the game for you!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/27344330/df3d51f357eb7a9cbec9a74a8b8daa5f86c5218a.png[/img]

One of the most popular complaints we receive since the game release is about partner’s AI. Now it's time to fix it. 

In 1.4.0 our aim is to make sure Rick is a real aid to the player, and not just a dummy carrying grenades. 

[h3]You can now access 1.4.0 Beta Version through Steam by choosing it in the BETAS tab (Right-click on the game in your library > Properties > Betas > Select open-beta > Download the update).[/h3]

Changes:

[list]
[*] Rick will return to the player automatically;
[*] Rick now looks for the potential threat himself — the spots from where the suspects are expected to appear;
[*] When meeting a suspect, Rick now independently takes actions to neutralize them:
[*] Asks him to surrender;
[*] In case of disobedience, he uses physical force;
[*] In case of aggressive resistance, he uses a weapon;
[*] In case the suspect starts to run away, the ally will pursue him as long as he considers it safe;
[*] Picks up weapons dropped from suspects;
[*] If a suspect gives themselves away, the ally will be ready for their actions;
[*] The player's commands still have the highest priority except when suspects are raising their weapons.
[/list]

Since this is a beta of an upcoming update, you can come across various bugs — we’d be glad to receive any feedback, which you can share with us through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/539470/discussions/0/3145179089266327845/?snr=1_2108_9__2107]Steam Discussions[/url]. Please note that this beta is only available for Windows.

We hope you enjoy this updated experience, and we’ll see you soon!

Greetings, officers!

While the next large update is on the way, we continue to polish the game on a regular basis. Here is a list of all the changes:

[olist]
[*] A bug that caused a game crash when selecting a map from the Steam Workshop has been fixed;
[*] Gamepad controls and detection in co-op mode have been fixed;
[*] Discord link in the main menu works again;
[*] Lots of Korean players complained about an inconvenient font. It has now become more readable; 
[*] Female characters now don’t refer to themselves as males in some languages;
[*] Some of the spelling errors and text bugs (when certain text blocks didn’t fit on the screen) have been fixed. 
[/olist]

Greetings officers!

We've fixed some of the critical issues with online co-op — all thanks to your feedback!

[h1]Changelog:[/h1]
- Fixed the critical error that occurred when the players tried to connect through Steam invites;
- Players are now able to properly join and invite to the game through Steam;
- Fixed the in-game "Invite friend" button;
- Fixed some of the issues with equipment loadouts;
- Fixed the critical error caused by both players simultaneously using borescope on the same door;
- Fixed multiple other smaller bugs.

Of course, these are not all bugs which were reported and we continue working on fixing them!

Don't forget to leave any feedback and ideas about Police Stories in the official [url=https://steamcommunity.com/app/539470/discussions/]Steam Discussion forums[/url], or join our [url=https://discordapp.com/invite/Dw4Jt5A]Discord Channel[/url] to hang out with other fans of the game!
